cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "hawkes-engine"
abstract: >-
  Multivariate Hawkes processes with exponential kernels for Python: a compiled
  likelihood and gradient, a maximum-likelihood fit with standard errors, two
  independent exact simulators, time-rescaling diagnostics, and a lookup of what a
  pre-registered simulation study measured about the fit's standard errors.
type: software
version: 0.3.0
authors:
  - family-names: Cheung
    given-names: Freddy Shi Chun
license: MIT
# Set to the tag date by the release checklist (docs/RELEASING.md). CFF requires
# this field for type: software.
date-released: 2026-10-24
repository-code: "https://github.com/freddysccheung-067/hawkes-engine"
url: "https://freddysccheung-067.github.io/hawkes-engine/"
keywords:
  - Hawkes process
  - point process
  - maximum likelihood
  - time rescaling
# There are two Zenodo records, and they are not versions of one another.
#
#   10.5281/zenodo.23613789  v0.1.0, deposited by hand (files: hawkes-engine-0.1.0.zip)
#   10.5281/zenodo.23620653  v0.2.0, deposited by the GitHub integration
#
# Each began its own series, so each has its own concept DOI, and neither concept
# DOI points at this version from the other. 0.2.0's own concept is 23620652.
#
# No `doi` or `identifiers` entry is set here, because 0.3.0 has not been archived
# and a DOI in this file is a citation to a record that exists. This is the same
# state 0.2.0 was in before its deposit: at that point the field was removed rather
# than pointed at 0.1.0's record, which would have told a reader to cite the wrong
# version. When 0.3.0 is deposited -- into the 23620652 series, so one concept DOI
# covers everything from 0.2.0 onward -- set `doi` and the two `identifiers` here,
# and update docs/release_notes_0.3.0.md, in one commit. See docs/RELEASING.md
# step 9. tests/test_release_metadata.py fails if only one of the two moves.
# The paper is not citable yet, so no author's paper entry is added here. It is
# deposited on HAL as `hal-05838093` and is in moderation: the record is not
# public, its public URL returns nothing to anyone else, and an unpublished
# identifier in a citation file would invite a reader to cite a record that does
# not resolve. When HAL accepts it, add it here as a `preferred-citation` with
# type `article`, the author, the title, the HAL URL and the acceptance year, and
# add the same line to `docs/STATE.md`. arXiv has not endorsed the `stat.ME`
# submission, so there is no preprint identifier to use in its place.
